From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Ninomiya <kainino@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 11:27:02 -0700
Subject: Add missing validation to copyExternalImageToTexture

copyExternalImageToTexture would ignore certain errors in
CreateExternalTexture (via CopyFromVideoElement which was incorrectly
pretending to be infallible).

Refactor several error-prone patterns so this is easier to do correctly
in the future.

Fixed: 560062638
Change-Id: I321c3a4256f8a14d4ddd505da2afb3f25ece7fab
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8415995
Reviewed-by: Brandon Jones <bajones@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Kai Ninomiya <kainino@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1699109}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
M150's CreateExternalTexture() still takes a media::PaintCanvasVideoRenderer* parameter and uses RecyclableCanvasResource instead of a shared-image lease. The std::optional<ExternalTexture> return type, the early returns, the null mailbox_texture check and the bool CopyFromVideoElement() plumbing were applied by hand onto that code; what is checked is unchanged.

